about.md:
  97      <h2 class="about-section-heading">Vision &amp; Mission</h2>
  98:     <p class="about-intro">Our approach to consistent mapping land cover from Earth observations was conceptualised through collaborations between Australia and Europe (including the United Kingdom) and national application was first demonstrated for Wales (UK) and Australia. Time-series comparisons of the land cover maps and the environmental descriptors from which they were constructed led to the subsequent development of evidence-based detection and monitoring of change impacts and driving pressures.</p>
  99  

earth-track-app-information.md:
   8  subtitle: "Earthtrack is a multi-module mobile application that was developed through Living Earth to routinely,
   9:         consistently and globally record information on land cover (including vegetation strata and dominant plant species) and land cover change
  10          with additional modules focused on country-specific habitats and fire. Earthtrack has been developed to support

  31          knowledge (e.g., citizen scientists, park rangers or academic researchers). Data submitted can be used directly
  32:         to validate mpas of land cover, habitat and change generated primarily from Earth observation data where these
  33:         use the same land cover and change taxonomies. These are, respectively, the Food and Agriculture Organisation
  34:         (FAO) Land Cover Classification System (LCCS) and Living Earth’s Global Change Taxonomy. "
  35          

