  44      description: "Continental mapping of Australia for 33 years"

  63    - title: "Dynamic Land"
  64:     description: "Quantitative land cover contents and map generation through Living Earth."
  65      url: "http://livingearthhub.org/our-projects/dynamic-land/"

  93    - title: "BIO_SOS"
  94:     description: "Land cover mapping from spectral data and derived metrics."
  95      url: "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/263435"

  98  
  99: Living Earth uses globally consistent taxonomies for classifying past, current and future land cover and change. The approach is simple in that maps of landscapes (e.g., land cover, habitats) can be constructed from environmental descriptors retrieved or classified primarily from Earth observations, and scalable in space and time because of the use of defined units or categories. Comparisons of the spatial datasets allows evidence on change impacts to be gathered, which can be combined with information on driving pressures to ascertain causes and consequences. This information, which is open, can inform decisions relating to the planning of future landscapes under a range of economic and/or climate scenarios, assess values of ecosystems, assess the realism of ambitions and ecosystem values, and monitor progress towards co-designed plans.

past-present.md:
  15  heading="Past & Present Landscapes"
  16: subheading="From knowledge of the past, we can inform the future but we need the tools to capture how we have historically shaped the landscapes of today. Earth observation data from satellites and aircraft give us a unique insight and so we have worked to develop a series of globally-applicable tools that allow us to describe, map and monitor land covers, habitats and ecosystems."
  17  data="past-present.index"

